Solaris correction after independent review of upstream pull request #430.
https://github.com/rdesktop/rdesktop/pull/430
Reject overlong local socket paths instead of silently truncating them.
Check fdopen, retain fgetc's int result and terminate at the current index.
Use one owner for the socket to avoid the proposal's double-close.
Recognize complete OK replies as success; reject incomplete reply lines.
Applicable to Solaris seamless mode; this is a local IPC path.

--- rdesktop-1.9.0/ctrl.c
+++ rdesktop-1.9.0/ctrl.c
@@ -198,7 +198,10 @@ len = sizeof(saun.sun_family) + strlen(s
 
 	/* test connection */
 	if (connect(s, (struct sockaddr *) &saun, len) != 0)
+	{
+		close(s);
 		return False;
+	}
 
 	shutdown(s, SHUT_RDWR);
 	close(s);
@@ -271,6 +274,11 @@ /* get uniq hash for ctrlsock name */
